# Project
Personal portfolio website of a software developer. Purpose: get a job.
Visitors are recruiters and technical interviewers. The site is the developer's
main professional presence (there is no LinkedIn profile).
Full specification: @SPEC.md. Content to display: @CONTENT.md.
Visual reference: the `design/` folder (Stitch HTML + PNG screenshots).

# Stack
- Next.js (App Router), TypeScript (strict, no `any`), Tailwind CSS
- Framer Motion only if needed, minimal use
- Deploy target: Vercel. No database: all content lives in `data/*.ts`

# Language and direction
- Site language: English only. Direction: LTR.

# Design
- Dark, technical theme. Use `design/` as a visual reference.
- Do NOT paste the Stitch HTML as is. Convert it into small React components.
- Put colors and fonts in the Tailwind theme (tokens), never hardcode them repeatedly.
- Palette: bg #0B0F19, card #111827, border #1F2937, text #E5E7EB,
  muted #9CA3AF, one accent color (cyan #22D3EE unless the design says otherwise).
- Fonts: Inter (or Geist Sans) for text, JetBrains Mono for tags, code and the name in the top bar.

# Structure
- Home page `/`: Top Bar, Hero, Projects grid, About, Contact, Footer.
- Project page `/projects/[slug]`: generated from `data/projects.ts`.
- Number of projects is flexible. Never hardcode a count. Render from data.

# Hard constraints (do not add these, even if the design suggests them)
- No navigation menu, no anchor links, no hamburger menu.
  Top Bar = name as plain text (left) + two buttons: Resume, Contact (right).
  On project pages the buttons are replaced by a "Back to projects" link.
- No logo.
- No LinkedIn links or buttons anywhere.
- No Experience / work history section.
- Education is a single line inside the About section.
- Project page has NO: challenges and solutions, results and learnings, screenshot gallery.
  Project page sections only: back link + prev/next, title + tagline, meta row,
  Live Demo + View Code buttons, main image or short demo, The Problem,
  The Solution, Tech Stack (with a reason per technology), bottom CTA.

# Code quality
- Server components by default. Use "use client" only when really needed.
- Use `next/image` for images. Always provide alt text.
- Semantic HTML (header, main, section, footer), valid heading order.
- Accessibility: WCAG AA contrast, full keyboard navigation, visible focus states.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Animations short (200-400ms).
- Mobile first. Check 360, 768, 1024, 1440. No horizontal scroll.
- Target: Lighthouse 90+ in all categories, no console errors.
- Small components, one responsibility each. No unused dependencies.

# Workflow
- Work one component at a time. Do not modify unrelated files.
- Before building a component, look at the matching file in `design/`.
- If the design and SPEC.md conflict, follow the "Hard constraints" above and tell me.
- Ask before adding any new dependency.
